    "explanation": "Rider and driver: this is an automated ruling, made without human review; either of you may appeal it once under POL-GEN-04. The rider's charge of $83.42 is refunded in full.\n\nWHAT THE TRACE SHOWS. The trip is TRP-02823, booked from Blk 412 Pasir Ris Dr 6 to Blk 7 Everton Park. The platform's optimal route was 2.4 km / 5.0 min. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-02823) records 67.2 km driven. Under POL-RD-01 the trace figure governs, because the trip record's 67.2 km is a rounded copy of the same measurement and may not be cited for the threshold test. The excess is therefore 64.8 km, or 2700% of optimal: both establishment tests (above 20% and above 0.8 km) pass, and the excess is also above the 50% and 8.0 km materiality tests. The deviation is ESTABLISHED and MATERIAL, and the rider's initial burden under POL-RD-08 (matching trip identifiers and a qualifying excess) is met on the trip record, trace and fare breakdown, which all carry TRP-02823 and the same 08:28:00 trip start.\n\nTRACE INTEGRITY. The trace is clean for policy purposes: 610 fixes at a 10-second sample interval, 100% coverage, zero gaps, maximum gap 0.0 s. None of POL-RD-07(a)-(c) fires, so the deviation stands on the trace alone and needs no independent corroboration.\n\nTHE DRIVER'S EXPLANATION. You said the rider changed the destination verbally. POL-RD-04 exonerates a detour only where the rider's instruction is recorded in the chat log, is timestamped before (or within 3 minutes of) the vehicle leaving the optimal corridor, and names a place or road the trace can be tested against via chat_message.waypoint_hint. The chat log for this trip (EV-CHAT-02823) holds zero messages, so there is no instruction, no timestamp and no waypoint_hint; the corroboration test cannot be run, POL-RD-04 is unavailable, and the excess is not reduced. Your statement cites no evidence ID, so under POL-RD-08 it carries no weight; and because it cites no artifact, it is not an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, so POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged and the case does not escalate on that ground. No endpoint amendment is recorded (pickup_amended_at, dropoff_amended_at and amended_optimal_distance_km are all null), so POL-RD-05 cannot be run; and the vehicle is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12 does not apply.\n\nTHE REFUND. The fare model is METERED, so POL-RD-02 governs. Recomputed fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 2.4 + 0.28 x 5.0) x 1.0 surge, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee + 0.00 ERP/tolls = 7.80. Refund = 83.42 - 7.80 = 75.62, rounded up to the nearest $0.05 = 75.65, which is 90.6% of the 83.42 charged. Because the refund reaches the 90% full-refund share, POL-RD-02 directs FULL_REFUND rather than a partial, and under POL-GEN-03 a full refund returns the whole contested amount: 83.42. The driver advocate's arithmetic (75.65) is correct and is the POL-RD-02 figure; it is the outcome label, not the arithmetic, that the 90% test changes. The whole charge of 83.42 is returned and the rider's claim for a full refund of 83.42 is accepted.\n\nDRIVER PROFILE. The POL-RD-06 check is required on a material deviation, but deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 210 completed trips in 90 days, so no repeat-deviation pattern is established. Neither the POL-RD-06(b) uplift nor the POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral is available. The lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter is not the trailing-90-day field POL-RD-06 names and was not used (POL-GEN-01).\n\nPASS-THROUGH CHARGES. The fare breakdown carries no ERP gantry lines, no tolls and no airport surcharge, and the trip neither originates at nor ends at an airport. POL-RD-09 adds nothing on top of the POL-RD-02 figure and there is no billing-integrity finding.\n\nNO ESCALATION. Confidence is 0.90, above the 0.70 floor; the trip identifiers match across the artifacts; no timestamps run backwards; the refund is below both the SGD 150.00 ceiling and the charged total; and no charge line is unmatched. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires. The traffic-advisory artifact EV-ADVIS-02823-01 is MISSING (weight 0.00, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT); no surviving claim relies on it and no traffic cause was asserted, so it carries no deciding fact and does not cap confidence. Both advocates' claims about that artifact were discarded for citing it without disclosing its impairment.\n\nCONFIDENCE. 0.90, capped by the artifacts that carry the deciding facts - the GPS trace, the trip record and the fare breakdown - each at weight 1.0.\n\nEXECUTION. The monetary effect of $83.42 exceeds the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so the ruling issues but the amount is held for release by a human reviewer under POL-GEN-05."
