    "explanation": "Rider and driver: the contested charge of SGD 83.42 is returned in full.\n\nFindings. The trip record (EV-TRIP-02823) and the GPS trace (EV-GPS-02823) describe the same trip TRP-02823, running from the recorded start at 2026-08-21 08:28:00 to completion at 10:09:30, and the fare ledger (EV-FARE-02823) is billed to the same trip. The rider's initial burden under POL-RD-08(a) is therefore discharged on matching identifiers and timestamps. Under POL-RD-01 the governing figure is the trace length, gps_trace.trace_distance_km = 67.2 km, not the rounded trip_record.actual_distance_km copy, against the booked optimal of 2.4 km recorded on the trip record: an excess of 64.8 km, which is 2700% of optimal. Both establishment tests (over 20% and over 0.8 km) pass, and the excess also exceeds 50% and 8.0 km, so the deviation is ESTABLISHED and MATERIAL. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07(a) to (c): 610 fixes at a 10-second sample interval, 100.0% coverage, no gaps and a maximum gap of 0.0 seconds. The deviation therefore stands on the trace alone and needs no independent corroboration.\n\nFare. The fare model is METERED, so POL-RD-02 runs and the refund is arithmetic. recomputed_fare = ((3.80 base fare + 0.75 x 2.4 km + 0.28 x 5.0 min) x the 1.0 surge multiplier read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee + 0.00 ERP and tolls = 7.80. The charged total is 83.42, so the refund is 83.42 - 7.80 = 75.62, rounded up to 75.65. That is 90.6% of the charged total and so reaches the 90% full-refund share POL-RD-02 sets: the outcome is FULL_REFUND of the whole contested 83.42, not the 75.65 partial.\n\nThe driver's account. The driver's statement that the rider changed the destination verbally is not supported by any evidence. POL-RD-04 requires such an instruction to be recorded in the chat log (EV-CHAT-02823), authored by the rider, time-stamped and identifying a place or road, and corroborated by the trace passing within